## Architecture Decisions Made (Phase 1)

### SSE for Progress

Server-Sent Events chosen over WebSockets:
- One-way data flow (server → client)
- Simpler reconnection handling with `Last-Event-Id`
- Native browser support via `EventSource`
- In-memory event retention for replay on reconnect

### Chunked Upload

5MB chunks with sequential ordering:
- Reliable over variable networks
- Progress tracking per chunk
- Resume from last successful chunk
- Server validates audio format on complete

### SQLite Database

Chosen over PostgreSQL:
- Single-user deployment scope
- No database server to manage
- ACID guarantees sufficient for this use case
- File-based, portable

