## Architecture Decisions Made (Phase 3)

### Edit Storage Strategy

Edits are stored in SQLite as discrete operations (not inline in transcript):
- Enables undo by deleting edit records
- Preserves original transcript for comparison
- Applied on-demand when retrieving or re-running

### Undo Implementation

Two-level undo:
1. Pending edits (client-side) - Removed from pending array
2. Saved edits (server-side) - DELETE from database

### Auto-save Strategy

Debounced 2-second auto-save:
- Batches rapid edits
- Prevents server overload
- Shows clear save status to user

