## Architecture Decisions Made (Phase 5)

### Two-Pass De-identification Architecture

**Decision:** Implement two-pass de-identification with human-in-the-loop name review

**Rationale:**
- De-identification LLMs can make mistakes in name detection
- Sociology researchers need control over what gets redacted
- Audit trail becomes more meaningful with human oversight
- Allows for iterative improvement of name lists

**Implementation:**
- First pass: LLM discovers potential names, stores intermediate results
- Human review: Researcher reviews and edits name list
- Second pass: Applies replacements using reviewed name list
- Audit trail: Complete record of all replacements with pass numbers

### PII Highlighting Strategy

**Decision:** Color-coded highlighting with tooltips showing original text

**Rationale:**
- Researchers need to see what was redacted without compromising privacy
- Different colors distinguish automatic vs manual redactions
- Hover tooltips provide context without cluttering the UI
- Toggle-able to avoid distraction when not needed

**Color Scheme:**
- Yellow: First-pass automatic replacements
- Orange: Second-pass automatic replacements  
- Red: Manual redactions
- Strikethrough: Overridden/restored text

---

